---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Privacy Policy | elderabusecalc.com';
const description = 'How elderabusecalc.com handles your data, including analytics, advertising cookies, the case-review form, and your rights under GDPR, CCPA, and other privacy laws.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: July 2026.</em></p>

  <p>elderabusecalc.com ("the Site") is operated by The Click Lab Agency LLC ("we," "us," "our"). This Privacy Policy describes what information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and what rights you have. We&rsquo;ve written it in plain language because the elder abuse content on this site reaches people in difficult circumstances, and clarity about data handling matters &mdash; especially because this Site includes a tool that connects you with attorneys.</p>

  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p>Short version: reading the calculator and guides is anonymous &mdash; no account, no personal information, nothing sent to our servers. Separately, if you fill out and submit the "Elder Abuse" case-review form, we collect your name, phone number, email address, and case details, and we share that information with attorneys or their agents so they can evaluate and contact you about your situation &mdash; this is a disclosed paid referral, not an accident. We use Google Analytics in a low-identifiability configuration to understand traffic patterns, and we display ads served by Google AdSense, which uses cookies to show relevant ads. You can opt out of personalized advertising, and of the attorney-sharing described above, at any time &mdash; see Sections 5 and 8.</p>

  <h2>1. Information you provide directly</h2>
  <p>The calculator on this Site is client-side. When you enter abuse-category, facility type, severity, state, and other details to compute an estimated recovery range, those values are processed in your browser and are not transmitted to our servers. We do not log calculator inputs. Reading the calculator, methodology, or guide pages never requires an account or any personal information.</p>
  <p>If you choose to email us, the contents of your email (sender address, body, and any attachments) are received by our email provider and retained for as long as needed to handle the conversation. We don&rsquo;t sell that email correspondence or add you to a mailing list. Please do not send identifying details about an active abuse situation by email &mdash; APS and the Eldercare Locator (1-800-677-1116) are the appropriate channels.</p>

  <h2>2. If you submit the case-review form &mdash; shared with attorneys</h2>
  <p>The homepage includes an "Elder Abuse" case-review form. If you fill it out and submit it, we collect the name, phone number, email address, and case details you enter, along with a timestamp and record of the consent language you agreed to. <strong>This form is the only way personal information leaves your browser on this Site.</strong> Submitting it is always optional; you can use the calculator and read every guide on this Site without ever seeing or completing it.</p>
  <p><strong>If you submit the case-review form, your name, phone number, email address, and case details are shared with one or more attorneys or their agents licensed to practice in your jurisdiction, so they can evaluate your situation and contact you about it.</strong> The Click Lab Agency LLC, which operates elderabusecalc.com, is not a law firm, does not provide legal advice, and does not vet, endorse, or guarantee the attorneys in this network. Submitting the form does not create an attorney-client relationship with The Click Lab Agency LLC or with any attorney until and unless that attorney separately agrees to represent you. The Click Lab Agency LLC may be compensated for these referrals. This arrangement is disclosed on the form itself at the point of submission.</p>
  <p>By submitting the form, you separately consent to be contacted by phone, text, and email &mdash; including by automated dialing technology &mdash; by The Click Lab Agency LLC and the attorneys or agents your information is shared with. That consent is not required to use any other part of this Site, and you can decline it by not submitting the form.</p>

  <h2>3. Information collected automatically</h2>
  <p>Like virtually all modern websites, our hosting provider&rsquo;s edge layer and our analytics provider receive some automatically-transmitted data from every visit. This typically includes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your IP address (used to determine approximate location for analytics, discarded after standard retention).</li>
    <li>Browser type and version, operating system, device type, and screen resolution.</li>
    <li>Referrer URL (the page you came from, if any).</li>
    <li>The pages you visit on this Site and how long you spend on each.</li>
    <li>Generic events like page-loads and outbound link clicks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
  <p>This Site uses a small number of cookies, split by purpose:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Strictly necessary cookies</strong> &mdash; storing privacy preferences themselves.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics cookies</strong> &mdash; Google Analytics cookies that distinguish your session from other visitors&rsquo;.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising cookies</strong> &mdash; Google AdSense cookies for ad personalization. You can opt out via Google&rsquo;s ad settings (see Section 6).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Google Analytics</h2>
  <p>We use Google Analytics 4 in a default-privacy configuration: IP addresses are truncated before storage, ad personalization signals are disabled where possible, and we don&rsquo;t merge GA data with personally identifying user profiles. Google&rsquo;s data handling for Analytics is described at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>. To opt out of GA entirely, install Google&rsquo;s browser opt-out: <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a>.</p>

  <h2>6. Google AdSense advertising</h2>
  <p>This Site displays ads from Google AdSense (publisher ID pub-6434377544325972). When AdSense renders an ad, Google uses cookies to (a) prevent fraudulent ad clicks, (b) frequency-cap which ads you see, and (c) optionally personalize the ads. You can review and adjust Google&rsquo;s ad personalization settings at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">adssettings.google.com</a> or opt out of third-party ad personalization via <a href="https://aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a> or (EU/UK) <a href="https://youronlinechoices.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.</p>
  <p>Opting out of personalized advertising does not stop ads from appearing; it stops them being matched to your inferred interests.</p>

  <h2>7. Other third parties</h2>
  <p>Beyond the attorneys or their agents who receive case-review form submissions (Section 2), Google Analytics, and Google AdSense, we don&rsquo;t sell or share visitor data with data brokers or anyone else. The only other third parties that may see data about your visit are our hosting provider&rsquo;s CDN and any third-party site you click through to (e.g., state APS pages, court opinions linked from guides).</p>

  <h2>8. Your choices and opt-outs</h2>
  <p><strong>The simplest opt-out for the attorney-sharing described in Section 2 is not to submit the case-review form.</strong> Nothing about your visit is shared with any attorney unless you complete and submit it yourself. If you&rsquo;ve already submitted the form and want to stop being contacted, email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> with the subject line <code>[OPT-OUT]</code>, or visit <a href="https://theclicklab.agency/optout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">theclicklab.agency/optout</a>. We will notify the attorney or agent your information was shared with and remove you from further outreach on our end.</p>
  <p>For advertising cookies, see Section 6.</p>

  <h2>9. Your rights under GDPR (EEA, UK)</h2>
  <p>If you&rsquo;re in the EEA or UK, the GDPR gives you several rights: access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, and objection. To exercise these, email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>. We&rsquo;ll respond within 30 days. Legal basis for our processing is generally (a) your consent &mdash; for non-essential cookies, and for case-review form submissions, given at the point you submit the form and withdrawable at any time by emailing us &mdash; and (b) our legitimate interest in operating, securing, and improving the Site.</p>

  <h2>10. Your rights under CCPA / CPRA (California)</h2>
  <p>California residents have the right to know what personal information we collect, to delete personal information, to opt out of "sale" or "sharing" of personal information, and to non-discrimination for exercising any of these rights. Two things can constitute a "sale" or "sharing" under California law: (a) advertising cookies, which you can opt out of via the Google ad personalization controls in Section 6, and (b) sharing your case-review form submission with attorneys in exchange for compensation, described in Section 2, which you can opt out of via Section 8. We do not sell or share data collected through anonymous site browsing alone &mdash; only case-review form submissions and advertising cookies are implicated. To exercise other CCPA rights, contact <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> with the subject line <code>[CCPA OPT-OUT]</code> or a description of your request.</p>

  <h2>11. Do Not Track</h2>
  <p>We honor DNT signals to the extent that, when DNT is on, we disable advertising personalization. We don&rsquo;t disable analytics on DNT alone. For analytics-off entirely, use the GA opt-out plugin.</p>

  <h2>12. Children&rsquo;s privacy (COPPA)</h2>
  <p>This Site is intended for adults dealing with elder abuse matters. The case-review form is not intended for use by anyone under 18. We don&rsquo;t knowingly collect information from children under 13. If you believe we have, contact us at <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> and we&rsquo;ll delete it.</p>

  <h2>13. Security</h2>
  <p>HTTPS on all pages, no user accounts, limited access to admin accounts and to case-review form submissions. Standard practices for a static informational site with a lead-intake tool.</p>

  <h2>14. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Our hosting provider and Google&rsquo;s services may process data outside your country (typically the United States). We rely on standard contractual clauses where required.</p>

  <h2>15. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We update this policy as needed. When we do, we update the "Last updated" date at the top. Material changes &mdash; especially anything affecting the case-review form &mdash; will be announced on the home page. Continued use of the Site after a change indicates acceptance.</p>

  <h2>16. Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
